      "title": "Event Loop Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Event Loop Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Stack and Web APIs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One call stack==, one thread",
                "A function ==runs to completion== before anything else",
                "{blue:Web APIs} (timers, fetch, DOM events) wait outside the stack",
                "When ready, they hand a callback to a ==queue=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Queues",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Queue",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Task (macrotask)",
                  "`setTimeout`, `setInterval`, I/O, UI events"
                ],
                [
                  "Microtask",
                  "promise reactions, `queueMicrotask`, `MutationObserver`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The Loop Rule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Run one task",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Drain all microtasks",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Render if needed",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pick next task",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Long synchronous loop holds the stack",
                "Timers, clicks, rendering freeze: nothing can be dequeued"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Microtasks drain ==completely== before render or the next task."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why does a long loop freeze the page?** Nothing can be dequeued.",
                "**Task or microtask first?** Microtasks, fully drained.",
                "**Who waits for timers?** Web APIs, outside the stack."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Execution Order and setTimeout",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Execution Order and setTimeout",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Order of a Script",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Sync code",
                    "sub": "whole stack",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Microtasks",
                    "sub": "drain all",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Timer task",
                    "sub": "one, then repeat",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Microtasks queued by microtasks run in the ==same drain==",
                "An endless microtask chain {red:starves} timers and rendering"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. setTimeout Rules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`setTimeout(fn, 0)` is ==not immediate==",
                "It queues a task after the stack and all microtasks",
                "Browsers clamp nested timers to about ==4ms==",
                "Equal delays fire in the order they were **scheduled**",
                "The delay is a ==minimum==, not a guarantee"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Classic Trace",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "console.log('A');",
                "setTimeout(() => console.log('T'));",
                "Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('P'));",
                "console.log('B');"
              ],
              "note": "sync, then microtask, then timer"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "A",
                "B",
                "P",
                "T"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Sync first, then ==all microtasks==, then the next timer. `P` always beats `T`, even with a 0ms delay."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Promises and async/await",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Promises and async/await",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. States and then()",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Three states: ==pending==, {green:fulfilled}, {red:rejected}",
                "A promise settles ==once==; its value never changes",
                "`then(onOk, onErr)` returns a **new** promise"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Handler does",
                "New promise"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Returns a value",
                  "{green:fulfils} with it"
                ],
                [
                  "Returns a promise",
                  "**adopts** its outcome"
                ],
                [
                  "Throws",
                  "{red:rejects} with the error"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Microtasks and await",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`then`/`catch`/`finally` callbacks always run as ==microtasks==",
                "Even when the promise is already settled",
                "An `async` function ==always returns a promise==",
                "`await` pauses **only that function**",
                "The rest resumes as a microtask once the awaited promise settles"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Sequential vs parallel",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "for (const x of xs) await f(x); // sequential",
                "const [a, b] = await Promise.all([f(), g()]); // parallel"
              ],
              "note": "start the promises first, then await them together"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "await in a loop",
              "text": "Each `await` waits for the previous step, so delays add up. Independent work: start it first, then ==Promise.all==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Error Handling Patterns",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Error Handling Patterns",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Errors in a chain",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Promise rejects",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "then skipped",
                    "sub": "every one",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "catch runs",
                    "sub": "returns fulfilled",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "next then runs",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A rejection ==skips every `then`== until a `catch`",
                "`catch` returns a ==fulfilled== promise, so the chain continues"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. async/await",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "try {",
                "  await load();",
                "} catch (e) {",
                "  log(e);",
                "} finally {",
                "  stop();",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "finally runs on success and on failure"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Unhandled rejection fires ==unhandledrejection== in browsers",
                "{red:Crashes Node 15+} by default"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where errors escape",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Code",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`then(() => { f(); })` no return",
                  "{red:Unhandled}"
                ],
                [
                  "`async` call without `await`",
                  "{red:Unhandled}"
                ],
                [
                  "`return f()` or `await f()`",
                  "{green:Caught}"
                ],
                [
                  "`throw` in executor",
                  "{green:Rejection}"
                ],
                [
                  "`throw` in later `setTimeout` callback",
                  "{red:Not caught}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==Return or await== every promise, and end each chain with a `catch`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Promise.all, allSettled, race and any",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Promise.all, allSettled, race and any",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The four combinators",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Fulfils with",
                "Rejects when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`all`",
                  "array, input order",
                  "first rejection, at once"
                ],
                [
                  "`allSettled`",
                  "outcome per input",
                  "never"
                ],
                [
                  "`race`",
                  "first to settle",
                  "first to settle rejects"
                ],
                [
                  "`any`",
                  "first fulfilment",
                  "all reject: `AggregateError`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`all` keeps ==input order==, not finish order",
                "`allSettled` item: `{status, value}` or `{status, reason}`",
                "`race` plus a timer = the ==timeout== pattern"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Timeout with race",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const timeout = ms => new Promise((_, rej) =>",
                "  setTimeout(() => rej(new Error('timeout')), ms));",
                "const data = await Promise.race([fetchData(), timeout(3000)]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Losers and interview point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No cancellation",
              "text": "Losing promises are **not cancelled**; their work keeps running."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**all vs allSettled?** all rejects on the first failure; allSettled never rejects.",
                "**race vs any?** race takes the first to settle; any takes the first success.",
                "**Does race cancel the losers?** No, they keep running."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Async Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Async Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Run order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Sync code",
                    "sub": "call stack",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Microtasks",
                    "sub": "then, await, queueMicrotask",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Timers, I/O",
                    "sub": "one task at a time",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Pick a combinator",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Every result",
                  "`Promise.all`"
                ],
                [
                  "Every outcome",
                  "`Promise.allSettled`"
                ],
                [
                  "First to finish",
                  "`Promise.race`"
                ],
                [
                  "First success",
                  "`Promise.any`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Loops and timeout",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Sequential==: await inside the loop",
                "==Parallel==: start all, await together",
                "==Timeout==: race the work against a rejecting timer"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "for (const x of xs) await f(x);",
                "await Promise.all(xs.map(f));"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "await Promise.race([work, new Promise((_, rej) =>",
                "  setTimeout(() => rej(new Error('timeout')), ms))]);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`forEach` with an async callback does not wait",
                "Promise left unreturned or unawaited: error escapes the chain"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always",
              "text": "Return or await every promise, and attach a ==catch==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What order does this print? `async function f(){ log(1); await null; log(2) } f(); log(3)`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "1, 3, 2",
                "`f` runs synchronously until the `await`",
                "the rest of `f` is a microtask, so it runs after the current script"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What prints? `Promise.reject(1).then(()=>log('a')).catch(()=>log('b')).then(()=>log('c'))`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "b, then c",
                "the first `then` is skipped; the rejection reaches `catch`",
                "`catch` returns a fulfilled promise, so the chain continues"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `items.forEach(async x => await save(x)); log('done')`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "'done' prints before the saves finish",
                "`forEach` ignores the returned promises, so errors go unhandled",
                "fix: `await Promise.all(items.map(save))`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In `Promise.all([p1, p2, p3])`, p2 rejects at 10ms and p3 takes 100ms. When does it settle, and what happens to p3?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "it rejects at 10ms with p2's reason",
                "p3 is not cancelled; it keeps running and its result is ignored",
                "use `allSettled` to get every outcome"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
